    {
      "id": "p0217-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In 2011, several regions of Japan were hit by devastating natural and manmade disasters. During this painful and turbulent time, many Japanese companies felt it would be inappropriate and tone-deaf to advertise their products on television between the constant news programs about the disasters. For this reason, ordinary commercials on television were often replaced with simple filler material.",
        "raw": "In 2011, several regions of Japan were hit by devastating natural and\nmanmade disasters. During this painful and turbulent time, many Japanese\ncompanies felt it would be inappropriate and tone-deaf to advertise their\nproducts on television between the constant news programs about the\ndisasters. For this reason, ordinary commercials on television were often\nreplaced with simple filler material.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12329945,
          0.31855714,
          0.67948915,
          0.41339286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.12197758,
          0.31784286,
          0.68081102,
          0.41446429
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          12,
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "2011 年，日本多地遭受严重天灾与人祸。在这段痛苦、动荡的时期，许多企业觉得，在不断播报灾情的新闻之间插入商品广告很不合适，也显得不懂人情。因此，电视上的普通广告常被简单的填充节目取代。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.12329945,
          0.31712857,
          0.69683608,
          0.41696429
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
